InMe - an Instagram Image Viewer Written In Scala/Play 2.0
=====================================

You can visit the demo at http://inme.herokuapp.com

Frontend dependency checks
--------------------------

The vendored jQuery asset is the official 3.7.1 release. It fixes the known
jQuery 1.x security issues while retaining the APIs needed by this legacy app.
Bootstrap 2.0.4 and Agility include small compatibility patches for jQuery 3:
placeholder '#' selectors, keyboard event detection, and collection lengths.
The application does not use jQuery Migrate or restore unsafe legacy behavior.

Run the frontend regression suite with Node 22.22.2+, 24.15.0+, or 26+:

    npm --prefix tests ci
    npm --prefix tests test

The tests check the official jQuery SHA-256, prototype-pollution protection,
HTML-prefilter behavior, login state, mocked feed/profile/pagination responses,
Agility rendering and bindings, and both Bootstrap builds. These are DOM tests
using jsdom, not a full browser, Scala/Play build, or live Instagram API test.
Test dependencies are development-only and are not served by the app.

Vendor sources and local patches are recorded in public/js/VENDOR.md.
